CERTORA VERIFICATION MUNGE — route result-mapping reads through getResult()
===========================================================================
Redirects every internal read of the `result[conditionId]` storage mapping to
the virtual `getResult(conditionId)` view, so the CVL summary of `getResult`
governs them. BaseMigrationMixin's read lives in BaseMigrationMixin_getResult.patch (split out so it
can be excluded selectively). Writes and the getResult bodies are untouched.

The neg-risk override derives sibling-NO / synthetic-Other results that are
never stored; routing getPayout/hasResult/reportResult through getResult makes
them observe those derived results (the property under proof), and the
migration read short-circuits to the raw mapping for migration conditions, so
that redirect is behavior-preserving.

Required by: NegRiskModule solvency + sanity scenes.
Apply:  git apply certora/patches/NegRiskModule_getResult.patch
Revert: git apply -R certora/patches/NegRiskModule_getResult.patch
Never commit the applied state to src/.

diff --git a/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol b/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol
index c3d9e1b..3f57d5f 100644
--- a/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol
+++ b/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ contract NegRiskModule is UUPSUpgradeable, Initializable, BaseModule, NegRiskMig
         // Resolver roles cannot resolve migration conditions.
         if (isMigrationCondition_ && hasAllRoles(msg.sender, RESOLVER_ROLE)) revert MigrationNotSupported();

-        uint256[] storage storedResult = result[_conditionId];
+        uint256[] memory storedResult = getResult(_conditionId);
         if (storedResult.length > 0) {
             // If the result being proposed by the resolver or bridge is different from the stored result, revert.
             // This is catastrophic and should never happen.
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@ contract NegRiskModule is UUPSUpgradeable, Initializable, BaseModule, NegRiskMig

             // Verify that the result being proposed by the bridge is equal to the result we just got from the CTF.
             // Something is wrong if this is not the case.
-            uint256[] storage resolvedResult = result[_conditionId];
+            uint256[] memory resolvedResult = getResult(_conditionId);
             if (_result.length != 2 || _result[0] != resolvedResult[0] || _result[1] != resolvedResult[1]) {
                 revert ExistingPayoutMismatch();
             }
diff --git a/src/modules/abstract/BaseModule.sol b/src/modules/abstract/BaseModule.sol
